	<name>Laminin-332</name>
	<description>Laminin 332, composed of the alpha3, beta3 and gamma2 chains, is an epithelial-basement membrane specific laminin variant. Its main role in normal tissues is the maintenance of epithelial-mesenchymal cohesion in tissues exposed to external forces, including skin and stratified squamous mucosa.</description>
